From d75c040db3f9982f65de7e4658918d733ec64c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:18:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] freedreno/a5xx: Set the sample count for the binning pass

The binning pass rasterised with whatever sample count the previous
batch left, as emit_binning_pass() never calls emit_msaa(), unlike the
tile, restore and sysmem passes. A multisampled render after a
single-sampled one was binned with the wrong sample count.

Fixes: cf0c7258ee05 ("freedreno/a5xx: MSAA")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46165>

Base-commit: b69adc2adfbfe3eb985bd66cd06c61ca719ae9ae
Apply in filename order within this project.
Source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/d75c040db3f9982f65de7e4658918d733ec64c2d
Backport validation: on Adreno 506, alternating 1x and 4x passes with
hardware binning on match the no-binning reference for all four individual
sample masks and the all-samples mask. The unpatched driver drops pixels.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c
index 31ba80332fd0..d038a8e27940 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_gmem.c
@@ -347,6 +347,8 @@ emit_binning_pass(struct fd_batch *batch) assert_dt
 
    update_vsc_pipe(batch);
 
+   emit_msaa(ring, batch->framebuffer.samples);
+
    OUT_PKT4(ring, REG_A5XX_VPC_MODE_CNTL, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, A5XX_VPC_MODE_CNTL_BINNING_PASS);
 
